# Third-party notices

AiPet itself is released under the MIT License (see [LICENSE](LICENSE)).

The release packages contain two programs, the pet (`AiPet`, `AiPet.exe`) and `aipet-hook`, the program the Claude
Code and Codex plugin runs. Both are written in Rust and built from the crates listed below, which are compiled into
them. The Windows installer also carries Velopack's `Setup.exe` and `Update.exe`:

| Component | Version | What it's for | License | Copyright |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| [Velopack](https://github.com/velopack/velopack) (`Setup.exe` and `Update.exe`, which vpk adds to the Windows installer) | 1.2.158 | Windows installer, updates and uninstall | MIT | Copyright © Velopack Ltd. |

Velopack's `Setup.exe` and `Update.exe` are written in Rust and built from crates that carry their own licenses.

The pet draws its text in the system's own fonts (Segoe UI on Windows, Noto Sans on Linux), which aren't part of
AiPet. The one font compiled into it is iced's small icon font (`Iced-Icons.ttf`, made with Fontello), which is part
of the `iced_graphics` crate and comes under that crate's license below.

The Aseprite files in `rust/crates/aipet-sprite/tests/fixtures/asefile/` (MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 Alpine Alpaca
Games) are test data only: nothing of them is built into AiPet. Their license is beside them.

The Hamster's design, and the ideas for its newer states, come from JLandbo's [hamster-pet](https://github.com/JLandbo/hamster-pet), used with its author's permission. That repository
carries no license, so this rests on the author's permission rather than a license.

## The Rust crates in AiPet and aipet-hook

The pet and `aipet-hook` are built from these crates, for the release targets (Windows x64, Linux x64 and arm64). The
versions are the ones `rust/Cargo.lock` resolves to, and the licenses are the ones the crates declare. Where a crate
offers a choice of licenses, the license texts it's listed under below are the ones AiPet uses it under. This file is
generated by [cargo-about](https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about) from `rust/about.toml` and `rust/about.hbs`:
run `scripts/check-notices.sh --write` to regenerate it, rather than editing it by hand.

